// teach 13: add with !Memory
// An obligation can lean on another declaration's parameter: the crossing
// of `inv` into `apply` claims Positive of what `apply` hands its callback,
// which is the parameter x of `apply`, and the claim stays open here. That
// parameter is no position the head of `main` can state, so it is never
// named as its need (D4: it was, on the gradient's first build).
type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn inv(n: Positive) = 100 / n

fn apply(f, x) = f(x)

fn main() = apply(inv, 0)
